# Honey Pie, bridge (figure 152.3)
# Paul's melodic bassline puts the chords in inversions: B under e (vi6/4), C# under A, D under G
# (I6/4), B under E (V-of-ii6/4). In bar 4 the D holds a beat and the bass walks G A B up to the
# C of bar 5.
#? Bass octaves are a guess (B2 up to D3, walking G2 A2 B2 to C3); the last D could be D2, a fifth down rather than a fourth up, and the whole line may sit an octave higher.
